Native census of the Save93 equipment run, 2026-11-11 06:45 build / AE 1.6.1170 / profile APB-CatchUp-Test, limiter 30 FPS.
Run folder build/catchup/cen-0645-30, 06:45-06:50. APB_GAMEPLAY_TRACE=catchup-census (accelerate on in all eight trials, VMCatchUp::SetCensus).
Test DLL APBGameplayTrace.dll sha256 aba1d4f65fc41dcc416f064c8399957d4724714df567d8893edcd4fb47e3e570.
First game run of the builds made on 2026-11-11 (04:11, 06:27 and 06:39 were never run). What this run was for: whether the helper
natives still pass the release rule now that their callback is checked, and whether Form.GetFormID is judged a read.

RESULT
- Install: "30 game natives and 14 SKSE natives count as reads". No "counts as a change" line (the new report of a listed name that
  fails the implementation check) anywhere in the log.
- Helpers: 17 functions of Math, StringUtil and Debug.Trace ran (3,258 calls); runtime_read on every call, runtime_change 0.
  Debug.Trace 227, Math.Floor 189, Math.abs 166, StringUtil.GetNthChar 2,203, the SKSE bit operations LogicalAnd/LogicalNot/RightShift 49.
  Debug.TraceStack did not run.
- Reviewed reads: all 44 listed names ran; runtime_change 0 for each. Form.GetFormID: 20 calls, all read (queued 2, extra 4, other 14).
- No native outside the list and the helpers got a read verdict. Auto properties: 185 names, 5,770 reads (getter), 198 changes (setter).
- Queued native calls in collected frames (queued + extra, properties left out): 16,051, of which 9,702 (60.4%) by natives judged reads.
- Eight trials, window in front 100% in each, guard_violations 0, no "turned off" line.
- After the window was closed the game left two crash logs (06:49:50, 06:49:53): execute access violation at 0x7FF5DF460000 / 0x7FF5DF450000,
  as after earlier launches of this profile; APB modules appear only in the module and plugin lists, not in the stack section.

NOT COVERED: the menu gate (this harness mode does not use it), NativePacing with Form.GetFormID (the trace DLL is built with the
Game.GetPlayer candidate and the player experiment was off), the release DLL itself, timings (a census run is not for timing).

